WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.380
In 1977, a severe drought struck Daphne Major, a small island in the Galápagos.

2
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.420
Most of its medium ground finches died.

3
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.500
The birds left had deeper beaks, on average.

4
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.580
Researchers had measured them before the drought.

5
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.340
So did the drought change the birds, or change which were left?

6
00:00:23.333 --> 00:00:26.053
Natural selection needs three things at once.

7
00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:31.693
First, variation. Variation means the differences among individuals.

8
00:00:32.973 --> 00:00:33.973
Second, inheritance.

9
00:00:34.653 --> 00:00:37.733
An inherited trait is carried in genes from parent to young.

10
00:00:38.733 --> 00:00:39.953
Third, unequal success.

11
00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:44.013
The differences change how many offspring an individual leaves.

12
00:00:44.833 --> 00:00:46.573
A mutation is a change in DNA.

13
00:00:47.493 --> 00:00:49.433
It is the source of new versions of genes.

14
00:00:50.813 --> 00:00:52.173
Selection does not make variation.

15
00:00:52.173 --> 00:00:57.273
It sorts the variation that is there, including new mutations as they arise.

16
00:00:58.333 --> 00:01:03.033
Fitness is how many offspring an individual leaves that survive to reproduce.

17
00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:09.653
An adaptation is an inherited trait that helps an organism survive and reproduce in

18
00:01:09.653 --> 00:01:10.673
its present environment.

19
00:01:11.693 --> 00:01:14.313
On Daphne Major, a deep beak was an adaptation.

20
00:01:15.413 --> 00:01:18.853
Large birds, especially males with large beaks, survived best.

21
00:01:19.713 --> 00:01:22.733
They could crack the large, hard seeds left after the drought.

22
00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:26.067
No bird's beak grew because of the drought.

23
00:01:26.887 --> 00:01:30.587
The birds that died were, on average, different from the birds that lived.

24
00:01:31.547 --> 00:01:36.267
Beak size is strongly inherited, so the next generation's beaks were deeper too, on

25
00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:41.567
average. Over many generations, selection like this can make a population better

26
00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:44.467
suited to its environment, but not perfectly suited.

27
00:01:45.307 --> 00:01:49.987
In later years, selection on these finches changed direction as rainfall and seeds

28
00:01:49.987 --> 00:01:50.987
changed.

29
00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:53.410
How can one species become two?

30
00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:58.890
A species is a group of populations whose members interbreed and produce fertile

31
00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:02.190
offspring in nature, and that rarely breed with other groups.

32
00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:07.730
Speciation is when one species splits into groups that no longer do that, or only

33
00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:11.410
rarely do. It often starts with geographic isolation.

34
00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:14.950
That is a barrier, such as a river, between the groups.

35
00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:19.390
On each side, different mutations arise and different traits are favoured.

36
00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:22.750
Separation alone is not speciation, though.

37
00:02:23.733 --> 00:02:24.873
Back to the question.

38
00:02:25.833 --> 00:02:27.893
The drought did not reshape any finch's beak.

39
00:02:28.613 --> 00:02:30.413
It changed which birds lived to breed.

40
00:02:31.333 --> 00:02:33.053
Their young inherited deeper beaks.

41
00:02:33.893 --> 00:02:38.733
One species can become two when separated groups change in different ways until they

42
00:02:38.733 --> 00:02:40.073
no longer interbreed.

43
00:02:41.333 --> 00:02:43.493
Selection sorts the differences that already exist.
